<LessonLayout title="Workbook — The Church, People of God" cic="CCC 748-870" scripture="">

<section class="content">

<h2>Student Workbook</h2>
<p class="big-question">For use after class or in a group. Print this page or work in your notebook.</p>

<h3>Remembering the Essentials</h3>

<ol>
<li>What does the word &laquo;Church&raquo; (from the Greek <em>ekklesía</em>) mean?</li>
<li>On what day was the Church born, and what happened at that moment?</li>
<li>What are the four marks or notes of the Church that we profess in the Creed?</li>
<li>What does it mean that the Church is &laquo;apostolic&raquo;?</li>
<li>What image does Saint Paul use to describe the Church as unity in diversity?</li>
</ol>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>For Reflection and Writing</h3>

<p>Answer each question honestly. There are no &laquo;correct&raquo; answers to these personal questions.</p>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">1. Describe an experience in which you felt the Church was truly a community, a family. What happened? How did you feel?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">It could be a retreat, a special Mass, a youth group, service to the poor, a pilgrimage, or simply a deep conversation with someone from your parish.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">2. Is there something about the Church that causes you difficulty, confusion, or even annoyance? How do you handle it?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Scandals, difficult teachings, the hierarchy, the failings of Christians... It's normal. What matters is how you process it. Do you talk to someone? Do you pray? Do you ignore it?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">3. What gifts or talents do you believe God has given you to put at the service of the Church? Are you using them?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">All the baptized have something to offer: time, knowledge, creativity, hospitality, faith, prayer, joy. What can you give? Is there a gift you have been keeping unused?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">4. The Church is holy but made up of sinners. How do you live that tension in your own life?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Do your own falls discourage you? Or do you learn to receive God's mercy and move forward, knowing that the Church is a hospital for sinners, as Saint Augustine said?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">5. How can you be a better member of the Body of Christ this week?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Think of a concrete action: pray for the Pope and your bishop, help at your parish, reconcile with someone, invite someone away from the faith to Mass, read a Church document, offer your day's work as an offering to God.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content" id="activities">

<h3>Practical Activities</h3>

<h4>A. Research your parish</h4>
<p>Find out when your parish was founded, who its patron saint is, who your diocesan bishop is, and what groups or ministries exist. If possible, interview the pastor or a layperson who has been there a long time. Write a short history of your parish and share something you discovered.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>B. Read Acts 2:1-4 and Acts 2:42-47: compare with your parish</h4>
<p>These passages describe the birth and life of the first Christian community. Read both texts and make two lists: (a) the characteristics of that community and (b) how it is lived (or could be lived) in your parish. What would you like your community to have that the first Church had?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>C. Get to know the martyrs</h4>
<p>Research the story of a modern martyr: the Coptic martyrs of Libya (2015), Saint José Sánchez del Río (Mexican Cristero), Saint Maximilian Kolbe (Auschwitz), or Blessed Miguel Pro. Read his or her story and write what most impressed you. What does their witness teach you about what it means to belong to the Church?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>D. Write a letter to a persecuted Christian</h4>
<p>In many places around the world, Christians are persecuted for their faith (Nigeria, North Korea, Pakistan, Eritrea, India). Learn about the current situation. Write a brief letter expressing your solidarity and promising your prayer for them.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>E. Pray for the Pope and your bishop</h4>
<p>Look up the name of the current Pope and your diocesan bishop. For one week, include them in your daily prayer. You can pray an Our Father and a Hail Mary for their intentions each day.</p>
<p>Name of the Pope: ____________________</p>
<p>Name of my bishop: ____________________</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>F. Discover the tilma of Guadalupe</h4>
<p>Look up information about Saint Juan Diego's tilma: what material it is made of, how long that fiber would normally last, and how long the image has remained intact. Note down three facts that surprise you. Read the story of the apparitions (the Nican Mopohua) and write what lesson it leaves you for your own mission as a member of the Church.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Memory Verse</h3>

<div class="bible-passage">
<p>&laquo;But you are a chosen race, a royal priesthood, a holy nation, a people for his own possession, that you may proclaim the excellencies of him who called you out of darkness into his marvelous light.&raquo;</p>
<p class="bible-passage__ref">— 1 Peter 2:9</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Prayer for This Week</h3>

<blockquote>
<p>Lord Jesus Christ,<br />
you who at Pentecost sent your Spirit<br />
and gave life to your Church,<br />
thank you for making me a member of your Body.<br />
Help me to love her as you love her,<br />
to serve her with my gifts,<br />
not to be scandalized by her wounds<br />
but to be part of her healing.<br />
Give me a missionary heart<br />
that knows how to bring your love to all.<br />
May I be a living stone in your Church,<br />
under the maternal care of Mary<br />
and in communion with the Pope and my pastors.<br />
Amen.</p>
</blockquote>

</section>

